Lands the WI-pavob clock ruling across all fifteen catalogues. Enumerated per language against named evidence (local toolchains where present, allowlisted upstream source otherwise) rather than the item's from-memory list; the enumeration surfaced a gap in a shipped catalogue (erlang lacked os:timestamp/0). Refusals recorded with reasons. Measured on 28 repos across all 14 changed catalogues, both arms sequential with fresh cache and arm-take proven: host_info_read chains 462 -> 901 (+95%), NO-HOSTINFO violated 16 -> 19, and the control claims NO-NET/NO-FSWRITE/NO-SUBPROC moved ZERO, which is the result that matters since this only adds host_info_read rows. Recall-increasing by design. Five languages moved zero for three different reasons, reported separately: rust/scala are correct rows unmatched because the analyzer emits module slot 'external'; java was a real enumeration gap (LocalDate.now) now added and confirmed on jenkins at 15 -> 34; javascript is explicitly UNVERIFIED. ADR-0016's boundary definition amended in place.
